t(53, 60, """cafés where people mix without restraints, and which has no amusement venues or shops selling forbidden things, how could this city dazzle people's eyes?

People will stroll in it .. Their happiness hormone will rise because they live in a clean, world-class environment .. They will buy what they need .. They will go back to their homes

What has ruined their worship here?

Worship is a personal decision; Islam came to settle pure monotheism in our hearts and to leave worship to people. How many abandon prayer in every society? How many women abandon the hijab? And how many matters of worship are abandoned today in those very same miserable, filthy cities with worn-out infrastructure .. So why did the filth of the cities not help push people towards worship?

So linking infrastructure with worship is an idiotic link, and the word idiotic (abit) is a classical Arabic word. What makes these people link worship with infrastructure is nothing but ignorance, lack of understanding, lack of experience in life and failure to grasp the reality of Islam, which they took to be the worship of dervishes swaying right and left night and day .. and lack of understanding of the human being, his needs and necessities, and that the happy person is closer to worshipping Allah and spreading his prayer mat at night compared with the miserable person who lives in a house full of dirt and dust and walks in a street that is all broken stones .. These people, sadly, mislead others with a premature, deficient and weak thinking, and the cause of its weakness is their weak experience in life and their turning, in this world, to matters that did not allow them to build a comprehensive and complete picture of the human being. They did not dive into the depths of the human soul; they saw the human being only from the surface, so they touched the shell of the human soul and did not dive into it to learn all its details. They learned some of the details of the human soul and thought they had known everything and encompassed everything

The upshot is that they misunderstood Islam itself and did not grasp its spirit
And the human being himself they understood in part and did not understand in full

And finally .. Poverty and filth are two great aids to moving away from Allah Almighty

Building cities of lower quality than the cities of other nations is a great aid to the Muslims' continued dazzlement by the other nations, and to the Muslim's continued feeling that he is small before the other nations, that he is weak before the other nations, that they are his masters, better than him and above him, and that he is their servant and less than them. This affects the souls of Muslims very negatively, and makes their long march of 100 years as captives of the West a continuous and prolonged march, changing nothing in their psyche; they go on saying the West is better than us, the West is finer than us, and they go on feeling inferiority and humiliation.
And this is enough""")

t(53, 1575, """The followers of Islam are not required to go on living amid filth in miserable cities, or in cities less clean than the cities of non-Muslims, on the pretext that Islam is a religion of worship .. This is the whispering of Satan and the speech of Satan, not the speech of Islam .. Satan only whispers into the souls of some, so they think they are speaking well and understanding well .. Muslims are not the scraps of the earth and its people, that they should live below others""")

t(54, 265, """If the virtuous city rested only on providing people's needs and covering their wants, no one would toil in life. But the virtuous city is founded on justice and equity, on equity and justice, on equality among people in justice, and on equality among people in equity; then on awareness and guidance, on building and preparation, and on industry and support, at times with gentleness and at times with firmness, and on the law that crowns all of this if it is respected and prevails. So all are equal, men and women, and no creature transgresses against another; it is not said, this is a woman, she has the right to do wrong, nor is it said, this is a man, he has the right to do wrong. So people understand that all are servants of Allah, to whom the rulings apply with justice and equity, and that in the virtuous city there is not only taking, but taking and giving. Whoever holds himself aloof from serving his society while able has taken and not given, and ability in men who are strong in body carries a higher due, except those excused by health, body, fatigue, exhaustion and age.""")

t(54, 780, """Women in public work and in social work
Most men do not understand something momentous about women in the mental, intellectual and psychological respect. I too did not know it until I discovered it! A woman from age 17 to 22 is one thing, from age 23 or 24 to 30 is one thing, from age 31 to 40 is one thing, from age 41 to 50 is one thing, from age 51 to 60 is one thing, and from age 61 to the end is one thing.

These changes that happen to a woman at the psychological level are not of the same nature as the psychological changes that happen to men at these same ages, because a woman's make-up is far more complex than a man's and roles are required of her in life towards husband, children and society. They are roles that turn violently, in sharp and severe bends, at every stage, unlike the man, whose roles, even if they turn, differ and change, do not shift, change and bend with the same sharpness as the bending of a woman's roles towards those around her. So a woman, in the case of newly married youth, will treat you from age 17 to 22 in a way that differs from age 23 to 30, the two being spouses who grow up together, and so on .. So many men witness these great, central psychological transitions that do not happen to them as men, and they wonder: has something happened? Has something changed? The truth is that nothing has changed but one thing .. What has changed is that the woman is as though created anew at every age .. In each new creation she carries with her a part of herself and not all of it, and she becomes very new in her new stage; then she moves to another new stage, throwing most of the old behind her and carrying with her something or some of it, and she puts on the new for the new stage, and so on .. So a woman, by her very make-up, is more able than a man to renew things and invent new forms of them, and so she is more capable than a man of perceiving fine details; she is created for details and the man is created for strategies .. This is the ABC of abilities .. The woman is detail-minded, a skilled executor .. and the man is a skilled strategist .. and if either of them is put in the other's place it will bring abject failure .. Every rule has its exceptions .. These psychological transitions in a woman's life qualify her to wear different personalities .. The 17-year-old cannot do well what the 40- or 50-year-old does well, and the woman of sixty, or 50 and 60, cannot do well what the 30-year-old does well, neither at the level of managing the family, nor at the level of forming mature social relationships around her, nor at the level of her administrative abilities. Talk of probing the depths of a woman's soul would be long, but this is an explanation sufficient for understanding the woman and her general social role.""")

t(54, 1915, """Good news for coffee lovers .. Perhaps, and Allah knows best, the coffee tree will bear fruit in new regions in the future, based on experiments that succeeded in countries and lands whose climate is not ideal for the coffee tree""")

t(55, 520, """As it was prophethood and messengership, and was sealed with the master of the children of Adam, our Prophet ﷺ, so there is no prophethood after him and no messengership until the Hour comes; and since the case was one of prophethood and messengership, the Companions did not scramble over it the way donkeys snap at one another, for they were an elite of creation alongside the master of the elite ﷺ, and so they were the best elite for the best master of the elite .. Then, when time had turned its full turn, an elite of that same number became rare among the men of the end time, because it is no longer prophethood or messengership but only sainthood (wilayah). But most erred, for they thought it was sainthood as befell the righteous saints, and so they thought it attainable and that the ego's share in it was possible and achievable, drawing on the fact that it is neither prophethood nor messengership .. So many of them today scrambled over it the way donkeys snap at one another (the righteous excepted), and said: it is neither prophethood nor messengership, so here we come for it .. They set their minds on it and it did not set its mind on them .. Then they set their minds on it and it did not on them .. Then they did and they did, and it did not .. Yes, indeed it is neither prophethood nor messengership .. but it is not ordinary sainthood .. nor is its station the station of ordinary sainthood .. So whoever is aware is safe, and whoever refuses has sought what is not to be sought, dared what should not be dared, and craned his neck towards what no human chooses of his own accord .. So he destroyed himself, since he thought the matter was easy and could be earned, and by Allah it cannot be earned .. and by Allah it is not easy! All this is the reason for what we see today: believing Muslim women, in numbers far greater than men, inclining to support the religion and uphold Islam and to speak sincerely of their love of supporting Islam .. For no Muslim woman today will aspire to this chosenness, which most of those misguided men thought was something earned merely by dreams that they fly in the air, or because one of them has two and a quarter moles on his calf and on his back 3 hooked moles with a quarter mole beneath them! We are in the age of wonders, by Allah.""")

t(55, 1335, """No one will fully understand the realities of things who has not been made apt for the thing .. He who was not made apt for medicine will mock doctors .. He who was not made apt for engineering will mock engineers .. He who was not made apt for religious knowledge will mock scholars .. He who was not made apt to be an undersecretary of a ministry serving people's interests will mock ministry undersecretaries .. and so on .. Everyone made apt for something different from others will mock, out of ignorance of it and of what the others say or do .. because he is in one valley and those made apt for that thing are in another valley .. But morals remain the judge, so that every person understands that as long as he was not made apt for a given thing, it is better for him to hold his tongue and occupy himself with what he was made apt for, because it is impossible for a person to grasp in all its aspects what he was not made apt for. This is one face of what humanity has been afflicted with through social media platforms, where everyone has become a doctor, everyone a civil engineer, everyone a nutritionist and everyone a politician who understands what is good for people, criticising everything so that he may be pointed at and it be said of him: this one understands! If a person removed the ego's share from his chest and gave his opinion, he would hit the mark .. If a person removed the ego's share from his chest and said, my opinion is such-and-such, his opinion would come out in kind, refined words far from mockery .. Mockery is a moral act when the misleading of people is clear and evident misguidance, and the misleader persists in misleading people, taking pride in his misguidance and presenting it as the sound divine method. Then the mockery is not mockery of the misguided servant, but mockery of the method and the thought, to alert people's minds that the criticism is real and not a mere opinion about an error, but criticism built on seeing the truth. That is why it came in an unusual and even unpalatable style, because it is not right that the voice of the people of falsehood be louder and their mockery of people's minds be accepted, yet when their sayings are mocked it is said: mockery is not morally permissible! And what of their mockery of our minds? Why did you let that pass for them? As for those who offer people ideas with no misguidance in them, only ideas that differ from our friend the genius who understands everything about managing people and their interests and whom no one can match in understanding what sets people's lives right, and who scoffs at something behind which there is no misguidance for people and no ruin: this is not of the kind that is mockery of evident misguidance; this is of the kind of chest that is filled with the ego's share and filled with regret over this world!""")

t(56, 605, """To my brothers the architects and the contracting companies of the future .. This is talk you may not have heard before, about the future of construction in the future of the coming world .. On the earth there are future capabilities which I do not think, and Allah knows best, will allow climbing more than 4 storeys for other than the elderly .. other than pregnant women .. and other than small children .. Apart from that, climbing to the fourth storey will be the hardest in any building .. The reason for these words is the expected collapse of electricity one year .. one day .. at a moment whose timing none knows but Allah Almighty .. And following the model of the Soviet Union in solving the housing problem, which is the chief preoccupation of some construction companies, the huge buildings containing hundreds or thousands of flats were the best solutions to the housing problem in the Soviet state .. As for rising more than 4 storeys, I do not advise it""")

t(56, 2005, """🔴 The heart of the matter is not that a person is wronged and crushed, and then is patient and pleased with his patience; rather, did this person turn into an oppressor after being exposed to oppression?! For very many did!
🔴 The heart of the matter is not that a person is wronged and crushed, and is pleased with his patience; rather, did this person turn into a spiteful envier after being exposed to oppression?! For many did!
🔴 The heart of the matter is not that a person is straitened in his destiny, his future and his life for a divine wisdom in it, and is patient and seeks his reward, mature and wise; rather, the heart of the matter is that this long straitening does not turn, once the straitening ends, into desire for this world and devotion to it! For many drowned in forbidden pleasures not permitted by the Shariah after the straitening ended!
🔴 The heart of the matter is not that a person is mocked for a stretch of time or for all time, ridiculed, plotted against and harmed, and is patient and remains humble, good-natured, sound of heart and disposition, and then Allah Almighty establishes him; rather, the heart of the matter is that after being established he remains humble, good-natured, sound of heart and disposition many times over, in thanks for Allah's blessing, for many people denied it after it came to them.""")

