t(65, 2010, """The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "The Hour will not come until the Euphrates uncovers a mountain of gold. People will fight over it, and of every hundred, ninety-nine will be killed, and each man among them will say: Perhaps I will be the one who survives." And in one narration: [Abu Salih al-Samman] said: "If you see it, do not go near it."
Narrator: Abu Hurayrah | Hadith scholar: Muslim | Source: Sahih Muslim

A brief comment: it is by no means necessary that the mountain be above the ground; the word mountain can linguistically denote a complete mountain in the interior of the earth, in the earth's crust itself, but the presence of water for thousands of years has prevented reaching it and seeing it clearly.""")

